    <title>KFKHFM</title>
    <description>Correction map of the hot-film air-mass signal, f(nmot8 720..6520 rpm, u8 rl 10.2..166.4 %). All 196 cells are 128 = 1.0 in this dataset, i.e. the correction is neutral. map_2d at CPU 0x5C430D (file 0x1C430D), 14x14 u8. FR module %GGHFM, p813. Name: STATIC. Scaling: STATIC. Read by FUN_00424cd0@0x424CD0. Name evidence: E3 #41: FUN_00424CD0 is %GGHFM's pulsation/correction block. Its last two statements are sVar1 = lookup_2d_u8(struct 0x5C42EF, nmot8, rl8) at 0x424F8C and 0x802856 = bVar2 * sVar1 * 2 (saturating), and 0x802856 is used exactly once, at 0x418CD0, as cand_mw_ml = (hfm_raw 0x7FEF9E * 0x802856) &gt;&gt; 15. So this map is the multiplicative correction of the hot-film air-mass signal over engine speed and relative charge. FR %GGHFM p813 declares exactly one label with that role and those inputs: 'KFKHFM nmot rl KF Korrekturkennfeld fuer HFM'. enumerate_maps.py; lookup_2d_u8; 1 call site(s): 0x424F8C; struct 0x5C42EF</description>
