  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x70" flags="0x30">
    <title>KLPBR_backpressure</title>
    <description>Cylinder back pressure over crank angle; dp = prist - ((KLPBR(x) * y) &gt;&gt; 17). The value is a scaled pressure whose divisor is inside the caller, so no unit is claimed. The x axis is read as the internal 3/128 degCA angle (0..177 degCA) - HYPOTHESIS. curve_1d_shared at CPU 0x5C72E0 (file 0x1C72E0), 12x1 u16. FR module %RKTI, p1826. Name: HYPOTHESIS. Scaling: HYPOTHESIS. Read by FUN_000ac42c@0x0AC42C. Name evidence: B6 #14 re/findings/injection.md S5.7; lookup_1d_g_s16_u16 at 0x0AC468. enumerate_maps.py; lookup_1d_g_s16_u16; 1 call site(s): 0x0AC468; B6: cylinder back pressure over crank angle, used to make dp = prist - ((KLPBR(x) * scale) &gt;&gt; 17). FR KLPBR. B6 #14, re/findings/injection.md 5.7</description>
