    <description>Ceiling of the relative charge request: 254 = 99.2 %. Every charge-domain variable in the torque structure is clipped to it. scalar at CPU 0x5C8C0C (file 0x1C8C0C), 1x1 u8. FR module %MDFUE, p724. Name: HYPOTHESIS. Scaling: STATIC. Read by FUN_000a9384@0x0A9384 FUN_00428fcc@0x428FCC FUN_004330b0@0x4330B0 FUN_004336e0@0x4336E0 .... Name evidence: E3 #41: u8 = 254, read at 21 sites; in FUN_004336E0 at 0x433880 the charge request is 0x803508 = min(2*v, this &lt;&lt; 8) and the same constant clamps 0x8034FC (0x434C00) and 0x8034FA (0x434AF4). Since 0x803508 is 100/65536 %/LSB (measuring id 2051 / id 8 handlers), one LSB of this byte is 256 x 100/65536 = 100/256 %, so 254 = 99.2 %. enumerate_maps.py; direct load; 21 call site(s): 0x0A944C 0x132BBC 0x132BE0 0x13503C 0x42915C 0x433280 ...</description>
