  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xFB" flags="0x30">
    <title>cand_KFMIRLUM</title>
    <description>Transitional KFMIRL twin, blended over the 100-step counter 0x7FD448: rlsol = (1-t)*KFMIRL + t*this, t = 0x7FD448/128. Its values are higher than KFMIRL's at high speed, i.e. it asks for more charge for the same torque during the transition. map_2d_data at CPU 0x5C91F2 (file 0x1C91F2), 12x16 u16. FR module %MDFUE, p724. Name: HYPOTHESIS. Scaling: STATIC. Read by FUN_00434c14@0x434C14. Name evidence: E3 #41: second map of FUN_00434C14, interp_2d_u16 at 0x434CA8 into 0x803520, weighted by t = 0x7FD448/128 (mul_shr15_sat(0x803520, 0x7FD448 &lt;&lt; 8) at 0x434D0C) while 0x5C9372 gets (1-t); 0x7FD448 is reloaded with 0x5D8FB0 = 100 at 0x465D8C while 0x7FE95B is set and counts down to 0 afterwards, so this map only acts during that window. FR %MDFUE p724 has no separate label for it (KFMIRL is instantiated several times), hence the descriptive suffix. enumerate_maps.py; interp_2d_u16; 1 call site(s): 0x434CA8; axes matched positionally to the axis searches in the same function</description>
