    <title>cand_KFMIRLINV</title>
    <description>Map over (relative charge 0..100 %, engine speed 560..6520 rpm), values 0..5103, almost independent of engine speed. Evaluated twice per activation, the second time at a charge rescaled by 200/0x8015AF. Both axes are proven; the value has no unit yet. map_2d at CPU 0x5C9938 (file 0x1C9938), 12x16 u16. FR module %MDKOL, p720. Name: HYPOTHESIS. Scaling: STATIC. Read by FUN_000e069c@0x0E069C FUN_000e0a0c@0x0E0A0C FUN_004125fc@0x4125FC. Name evidence: E3 #41: FUN_000E069C is three lines long: 0x8015D0 = lookup_2d_u16(0x5C98FC, nmot_w, 0x8034FA); 0x8015CA = mul_div_sat(0x8034FA, 200, u8@0x8015AF); 0x8015CE = lookup_2d_u16(0x5C98FC, nmot_w, 0x8015CA). The same map is therefore evaluated twice, once at the real charge and once at a charge rescaled by 200/0x8015AF - the shape of a normalisation to standard conditions. Axes proven: 0x5C9900 (16 u16 = 2240..26080 = 560..6520 rpm at 0.25 rpm/LSB) and 0x5C9920 (12 u16 = 0, 6554, 9830, 13107, 16384, 19661, 26214, 32768, 39322, 45875, 52429, 65529 = 0, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70, 80, 100 % at the 100/65536 %/LSB of 0x8034FA). The output unit is NOT established - see calibration_names.md section 9.6. enumerate_maps.py; lookup_2d_u16; 4 call site(s): 0x0E06B4 0x0E06E0 0x0E0D90 0x412654; struct 0x5C98FC</description>
