  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x42B" flags="0x30">
    <title>cand_KLFRLMXT</title>
    <description>Temperature-dependent charge-limit factor, 115.5..117.75 degC. All four points are 255 (&gt;= 1.0), which switches the limit off. curve_1d at CPU 0x5D7EBF (file 0x1D7EBF), 4x1 u8. FR module %MDKOL, p720. Name: HYPOTHESIS. Scaling: STATIC. Read by FUN_000fc250@0x0FC250. Name evidence: E3 #41: lookup_1d_u8(struct 0x5D7EBA, 0x802363) at 0x0FC2FC; the struct is {u8 n=4; u8 axis[4] = 218, 219, 220, 221; u8 val[4] = 255, 255, 255, 255}. 0x802363 is 0x7FD3F7 (or 0x80229B when 0x5D7ED6 bit 0 is set), the u8 temperature of rail.md section 3.2, so the axis is 115.5, 116.25, 117.0, 117.75 degC. The result feeds 0x802362, and 0x802360 = 0xFFFF as soon as 0x802362 &gt;= 0x80, so a value of 255 means 'no limit'. enumerate_maps.py; lookup_1d_u8; 1 call site(s): 0x0FC324; struct 0x5D7EBA</description>
